schema: concept-lineage
object:
  title: "Evergreen notes / seedling-budding-evergreen maturity taxonomy"
  type: concept-lineage
  short_description: >-
    A practice of writing notes that "evolve, contribute, and accumulate over
    time, across projects" (Andy Matuschak's definition), paired with a
    visible maturity label — seedling, budding, evergreen — so a reader can
    tell at a glance whether they're looking at a rough sketch or a settled
    idea (Maggie Appleton's digital-garden taxonomy).
  source_traditions:
    - Andy Matuschak's "Evergreen notes" essay
    - Maggie Appleton's digital-garden maturity taxonomy ("Growing the Evergreens")
    - Quartz (static-site generator) frontmatter maturity/publish flags
  toolkit_usage: >-
    Cited in the article as the ethic behind composting: a dying page may
    contain a few paragraphs that were never about the deprecated content at
    all (working agreements, a good rationale, hard-won gotchas), and
    composting means lifting those into pages that carry the same growth-
    state signal so readers can trust what they're reading.
  adjacent_meanings:
    - the Toolkit's own K1 maturity axis (raw/held/draft/candidate/source-linked/reviewed/...), a different, more granular ladder for a different purpose (trust/review state, not editorial roughness)
  important_distinctions:
    - >-
      "seedling/budding/evergreen" signals *editorial* maturity (how settled
      the writing is); it is not the same axis as the Toolkit's K1
      maturity/public_use/lifecycle_state model, though both aim to make
      trust visible rather than assumed.
  tensions: []
  risks_of_flattening: >-
    Treating maturity labeling as decoration rather than a load-bearing trust
    signal misses the article's point: the label is what lets a reader tell a
    rough sketch from a settled idea without asking anyone.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/archive-compost.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
  work_order: wo-d6e9e6e15257
  source_lineage: archive-compost.md
